WEBVTT

1
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:57,736
Hello, how are you?

2
00:00:57,903 --> 00:00:59,236
Hello, Esteban.
Pleased to see you.

3
00:01:00,736 --> 00:01:03,570
- Can I take your coat.
- No, I'd rather keep it.

4
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:20,320
Would you like a drink?

5
00:01:20,403 --> 00:01:23,986
Sparkling water,
with ice and lemon, please.

6
00:01:42,903 --> 00:01:44,986
- Hello.
- How are you?

7
00:01:46,236 --> 00:01:49,570
- Do you have a reservation?
- Yes, for Esteban Martínez I think.

8
00:01:49,736 --> 00:01:52,653
- Can I take your coat?
- Yes, hold on.

9
00:01:52,903 --> 00:01:56,570
- And your purse, if you like.
- Sure.

10
00:01:59,403 --> 00:02:01,433
- This way, please.
- Thank you.

11
00:02:02,653 --> 00:02:04,903
- Hello.
- How are you?

12
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:06,653
Fine, thanks.

13
00:02:08,153 --> 00:02:09,236
That's good.

14
00:02:09,236 --> 00:02:11,486
- I'm pleased to see you.
- Same here.

15
00:02:11,736 --> 00:02:12,986
- This place is lovely.
- You like it?

16
00:02:13,153 --> 00:02:16,653
- Yes.
- It's very pleasant, very quiet.

17
00:02:17,403 --> 00:02:19,403
I came here just the other day...

18
00:02:19,903 --> 00:02:21,903
Do you come here much?

19
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:24,653
Well, I've just moved, so...

20
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,570
- Hello.
- Welcome.

21
00:02:26,736 --> 00:02:28,320
- Thank you.
- Can I get you a drink?

22
00:02:28,403 --> 00:02:29,903
A beer, please.

23
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:31,820
Thank you.

24
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:34,736
- How are you?
- I'm fine.

25
00:02:34,903 --> 00:02:37,653
I'm fine, and you?

26
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,736
I'm fine too.

27
00:02:42,486 --> 00:02:44,070
- Well...
- What shall we eat?

28
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:45,820
The green beans here
are really good.

29
00:02:45,986 --> 00:02:47,320
I tried them the other day.

30
00:02:50,153 --> 00:02:52,820
Fish is fine with me.

31
00:02:54,736 --> 00:02:56,320
It all sounds good.

32
00:02:56,486 --> 00:02:58,653
- Are you ready to order?
- Yes.

33
00:03:00,236 --> 00:03:01,070
Green beans...

34
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,320
- And the grouper.
- Great.

35
00:03:03,570 --> 00:03:05,736
Do you think that's fine?
Will that be enough for us?

36
00:03:05,903 --> 00:03:07,320
Yes, I think so.

37
00:03:11,653 --> 00:03:12,820
You're looking really good.

38
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:14,570
Oh, thank you.

39
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:18,403
I'm very well, Emilia,
I'm very well.

40
00:03:19,653 --> 00:03:22,403
- Are you well?
- Yes, I just told you I'm well.

41
00:03:22,903 --> 00:03:25,736
- Have you come from home?
- Yes, I have.

42
00:03:25,903 --> 00:03:28,320
- Do you work every day?
- Normally, Tuesday to Sunday.

43
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:31,903
And yes, I'm working in a bar.

44
00:03:32,486 --> 00:03:33,903
But it's good.

45
00:03:34,070 --> 00:03:37,070
Of all the places I've been,
it's where I'm most comfortable.

46
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,403
- Do they treat you well?
- Yes.

47
00:03:40,403 --> 00:03:41,986
And that's all really.

48
00:03:42,153 --> 00:03:46,403
I'm there, and I'm ok.

49
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:49,653
You came back
two months ago, right?

50
00:03:49,903 --> 00:03:55,070
Yes, I came back
for personal reasons too.

51
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:59,070
I wanted to get out of New York.

52
00:03:59,403 --> 00:04:01,320
I didn't want to be there.

53
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:04,070
I want my children
to have a relationship with...

54
00:04:04,403 --> 00:04:06,653
Unfortunately green beans
are off the menu.

55
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,320
We have to change the first course.

56
00:04:11,903 --> 00:04:13,736
What a pity, they were delicious.

57
00:04:13,903 --> 00:04:15,486
- Yes, I'm sorry.
- Don't worry.

58
00:04:16,403 --> 00:04:18,653
- Peas?
- We have the shrimp you liked...

59
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,653
What do you recommend?

60
00:04:20,986 --> 00:04:24,070
- I'd go for the sea bass tartare.
- That will be fine.

61
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,903
Thank you.

62
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,820
What was I saying?
Yes, my children...

63
00:04:27,986 --> 00:04:31,820
My children are happy
and Alice is...

64
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:35,903
She's an editor
so she can work anywhere.

65
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:38,570
She edits book, novels...?

66
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:41,986
Yes, she edits novels, fiction.

67
00:04:42,153 --> 00:04:45,403
I'd love you to meet her.

68
00:04:45,653 --> 00:04:50,653
She's a very important woman
in my life, in my process.

69
00:04:51,903 --> 00:04:54,653
- Do you have a partner?
- No.

70
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,986
I'm happy.
I'm perfectly fine.

71
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,903
But no, I don't have a partner.

72
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:04,653
- I've got a roommate.
- You do?

73
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:06,986
We've been friends for ages.

74
00:05:07,570 --> 00:05:08,403
It's all good.

75
00:05:08,653 --> 00:05:10,153
Are you here for the film

76
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:13,070
or so your children
can see Spanish culture?

77
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:15,320
For both reasons, really.

78
00:05:15,486 --> 00:05:19,236
The film takes place in Spain
so it has to be shot here,

79
00:05:19,403 --> 00:05:21,570
because of what it's about,
I'll tell you more later.

80
00:05:21,736 --> 00:05:25,403
But I also wanted to get out
of there, to be somewhere...

81
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:32,736
to be here.

82
00:05:32,736 --> 00:05:33,570
and to be...

83
00:05:33,736 --> 00:05:35,986
near you, too.

84
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:43,320
I really appreciate you
getting in touch.

85
00:05:43,403 --> 00:05:44,653
It's been a long time.

86
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:46,570
- Thirteen years.
- Thirteen.

87
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,986
- A very long time.
- A long time, yes.

88
00:05:55,236 --> 00:05:55,903
And, well...

89
00:05:57,736 --> 00:06:00,820
You'll be wondering
why I called you.

90
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:02,986
I am kind of curious.

91
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:07,570
I want to start with...

92
00:06:07,736 --> 00:06:10,653
What do you know about
the conflict in Western Sahara?

93
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:12,653
I'm sure you know something.

94
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:15,320
What is this, an exam or something?

95
00:06:15,486 --> 00:06:19,403
It's to introduce the story
I want to tell...

96
00:06:19,653 --> 00:06:21,986
But to do that you have to know...

97
00:06:23,403 --> 00:06:24,320
the setting.

98
00:06:24,653 --> 00:06:26,320
About the Sahara?

99
00:06:26,486 --> 00:06:29,986
I know that it was
a Spanish colony.

100
00:06:31,403 --> 00:06:32,986
But not much more.

101
00:06:33,153 --> 00:06:36,070
After the Berlin Conference
they were given territory.

102
00:06:36,403 --> 00:06:39,320
And they went there.
Well, Spain withdrew at one point

103
00:06:39,570 --> 00:06:42,570
and now those people
have been left to their fate.

104
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:46,070
To sum up, we've left them
to their fate, abandoned them.

105
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:51,070
As you know about the Sahara,
I'll tell you the film.

106
00:06:52,570 --> 00:06:54,903
The film is called "Desert".

107
00:06:55,986 --> 00:06:58,820
And that historical setting
in the Sahara

108
00:06:58,986 --> 00:07:01,570
is where the film takes place...

109
00:07:01,736 --> 00:07:03,736
The film I want to offer you.

110
00:07:04,486 --> 00:07:06,320
The year is 1932,

111
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:10,736
Spain is a colonizing power
in Western Sahara,

112
00:07:10,903 --> 00:07:13,486
there is a fort,

113
00:07:13,486 --> 00:07:15,820
there is a detachment
of the Spanish army,

114
00:07:15,986 --> 00:07:18,820
Bernardo is the lieutenant there,

115
00:07:18,986 --> 00:07:21,820
he's from Madrid.

116
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:26,736
And gradually a relationship grows
between this lieutenant

117
00:07:26,903 --> 00:07:29,653
and Salek, who is a shepherd,

118
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:33,070
and a leader of the Sahrawi tribe
closest to the fort.

119
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:37,403
A nice relationship emerges
between these men.

120
00:07:37,903 --> 00:07:40,403
Just then,
Gabriela appears on the scene.

121
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:42,903
She is a 30- year- old woman

122
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:45,903
who was told at the age of 20
that she couldn't have children.

123
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:50,986
She meets Bernardo
at an academy party

124
00:07:51,653 --> 00:07:54,070
and after six months
they decide to get married.

125
00:07:54,403 --> 00:07:56,070
It's a second marriage for him,

126
00:07:56,320 --> 00:08:00,486
and Gabriela feels that
it's the exact reason

127
00:08:00,736 --> 00:08:03,653
to escape from the suffocating,

128
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,820
almost prison-like atmosphere
in Madrid

129
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:07,986
and have an adventure in the desert

130
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:12,320
and unleash her needs as a woman.

131
00:08:12,653 --> 00:08:14,486
By the way, do you know...

132
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,736
Comet?

133
00:08:15,986 --> 00:08:18,403
- Comet? The actor?
- Yes.

134
00:08:18,653 --> 00:08:19,820
Well, not personally.

135
00:08:19,986 --> 00:08:23,820
He's playing Bernardo,
the Spanish lieutenant,

136
00:08:23,986 --> 00:08:27,903
your husband,
if you decide to play Gabriela.

137
00:08:28,403 --> 00:08:31,236
- I really like him.
- He's very good.

138
00:08:31,403 --> 00:08:32,986
Then we have the couple,

139
00:08:33,153 --> 00:08:34,903
Captain Moraza
and his wife Mercedes,

140
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:37,903
played by Barbara Luque
and Raul Oyarzun.

141
00:08:38,736 --> 00:08:40,403
What a cast!

142
00:08:41,570 --> 00:08:42,820
Yes, it's really good.

143
00:08:42,986 --> 00:08:44,986
It's a story

144
00:08:45,653 --> 00:08:48,653
about betrayal,
a story about abandonment,

145
00:08:49,736 --> 00:08:51,653
it's a story about love,

146
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:56,820
about people who can't
look each other in the eye.

147
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:59,403
We're shooting in Fuerteventura,

148
00:08:59,653 --> 00:09:02,320
because we can't shoot
in the Sahara.

149
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:04,736
Sorry, it's just that I'm a bit...

150
00:09:06,736 --> 00:09:09,320
I'm shocked, I'm surprised,

151
00:09:09,403 --> 00:09:12,820
that you're offering me
something like this.

152
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:20,653
Could I have a red wine, please?

153
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,070
Look...

154
00:09:25,903 --> 00:09:27,903
I can say...

155
00:09:29,403 --> 00:09:31,070
Oh, shit, this is really spicy.

156
00:09:32,403 --> 00:09:34,570
- It isn't spicy.
- It is spicy.

157
00:09:35,653 --> 00:09:37,070
I don't think it is.

158
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,820
I've been seeing a lot

159
00:09:39,986 --> 00:09:42,403
of your work, your series

160
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:52,570
"Secret Files" was one,
you were a police in that.

161
00:09:52,736 --> 00:09:55,903
Beyond rating the series
or films in themselves,

162
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:59,403
that doesn't matter,
what I feel is that,

163
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:04,070
what you bring to the table
is always very interesting.

164
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:06,320
In that series I mentioned,

165
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:08,653
it's hard to be good
in such a bad series.

166
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,986
I mean, people do what they can,

167
00:10:11,153 --> 00:10:15,570
but when the text is so difficult,
so stiff, so cliched,

168
00:10:15,736 --> 00:10:20,070
and so vague,
everyone sounds the same,

169
00:10:20,403 --> 00:10:23,320
it's hard to find a light,

170
00:10:23,486 --> 00:10:26,820
a spark of truth,
something unexpected,

171
00:10:26,986 --> 00:10:31,820
and you manage it several times.

172
00:10:34,486 --> 00:10:36,653
I wouldn't lie to you about this.

173
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,403
- No, I think it's good.
- It's true.

174
00:10:40,236 --> 00:10:41,403
It's perfectly...

175
00:10:42,653 --> 00:10:45,403
It's perfectly logical,
given where you come from.

176
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:48,320
You're the daughter
of an actress and a director.

177
00:10:48,486 --> 00:10:52,070
There's something
in the genes that works,

178
00:10:52,403 --> 00:10:55,320
that's alive, that understands.

179
00:10:55,486 --> 00:10:57,403
I feel that I still...

180
00:10:57,570 --> 00:11:02,486
haven't had the opportunity
to really work.

181
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:05,903
I've served
plenty of lunches, but...

182
00:11:06,403 --> 00:11:10,320
I've worked,
of course, done things...

183
00:11:10,403 --> 00:11:11,986
I'm not very proud
of what I've done,

184
00:11:12,153 --> 00:11:16,320
But I feel I haven't been able
to do a character arc,

185
00:11:18,486 --> 00:11:21,820
a character with contradictions,

186
00:11:21,986 --> 00:11:24,653
who had any kind of substance...

187
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:29,736
I've tried to but...

188
00:11:29,903 --> 00:11:32,570
Do you go to casting calls?
I'm surprised you don't work more.

189
00:11:32,736 --> 00:11:34,070
Quite a few, yes.

190
00:11:34,403 --> 00:11:37,320
- Quite a few what?
- Quite a few casting calls.

191
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,403
Well, look,

192
00:11:42,403 --> 00:11:45,653
what I've told you is the film,

193
00:11:45,903 --> 00:11:48,403
that I'm going to make,

194
00:11:48,986 --> 00:11:53,486
and I'd love you to play
the character of Gabriela.

195
00:11:54,736 --> 00:11:57,570
Because I think
you can do a very good job.

196
00:11:57,736 --> 00:12:00,570
And because I think I can help you.

197
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,820
That's something
I'd like to do because...

198
00:12:03,986 --> 00:12:06,236
I haven't helped you...

199
00:12:12,903 --> 00:12:16,320
It would be nice
to be able to help you.

200
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:19,403
But if you say yes,

201
00:12:20,403 --> 00:12:22,570
I'm going to be tough.

202
00:12:22,736 --> 00:12:23,820
I'll be directing you,

203
00:12:23,986 --> 00:12:26,736
I'll be demanding
just like with the other actors.

204
00:12:26,903 --> 00:12:28,570
Yeah, I know, I can imagine.

205
00:12:28,903 --> 00:12:30,903
I wouldn't expect anything less.

206
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:35,403
Because I know you've got it.

207
00:12:40,403 --> 00:12:42,986
There's something
I wanted to ask you.

208
00:12:43,570 --> 00:12:47,986
The people on the film,
do they know

209
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,486
that you're my father,
what do they know?

210
00:12:51,653 --> 00:12:54,903
They'll know
what they have to know.

211
00:12:55,070 --> 00:12:57,320
That will never be a problem.

212
00:12:57,570 --> 00:12:59,070
It might be for me though...

213
00:13:00,153 --> 00:13:02,820
I want to reassure you
about that...

214
00:13:03,903 --> 00:13:06,903
Yes, I'm helping my daughter, but

215
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:11,903
that isn't at odds with the actress
I think should play the role.

216
00:13:12,070 --> 00:13:13,820
You're the actress
I want for the role,

217
00:13:13,986 --> 00:13:15,653
and, in addition,
you're my daughter.

218
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:18,403
People will think whatever.

219
00:13:18,570 --> 00:13:22,736
Some will naturally think
that it's favoritism.

220
00:13:22,903 --> 00:13:24,153
So what?

221
00:13:24,736 --> 00:13:26,570
What do we care
about what people think?

222
00:13:26,736 --> 00:13:28,736
The important thing
is to concentrate on the work,

223
00:13:28,903 --> 00:13:31,570
and focus on that,
we go step by step,

224
00:13:31,736 --> 00:13:36,403
and everything
will come together.

225
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:42,653
I'm really grateful, but

226
00:13:43,903 --> 00:13:46,736
I just want to think about it
for a while.

227
00:13:46,903 --> 00:13:50,403
You have to understand
that it's strange for me.

228
00:13:50,653 --> 00:13:52,986
I haven't seen you for a long time.

229
00:13:57,653 --> 00:14:02,653
now I'm fine but
I want to think it over.

230
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:06,570
I'm truly grateful
but I want to think it over.

231
00:14:12,403 --> 00:14:14,653
Have you finished yours?

232
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:17,070
If it's spicy, don't eat it.

233
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,403
You know what I just remembered?

234
00:14:25,653 --> 00:14:28,653
That lunch in Formentera.

235
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:34,070
Seeing you
eating brought it to mind.

236
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:39,070
We had fun there, didn't we?

237
00:14:39,570 --> 00:14:42,320
I didn't like that rice at all.

238
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:45,070
It didn't turn out well, did it?

239
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:47,820
No, I just didn't like it.

240
00:14:48,070 --> 00:14:51,070
I was in no fit state
to make rice back then.

241
00:14:52,903 --> 00:14:55,070
But I tried anyway...

242
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:01,903
How's Charo?

243
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:05,903
Fine, she's fine.

244
00:15:06,070 --> 00:15:08,403
- Yes?
- Yes.

245
00:15:08,403 --> 00:15:08,903
I'm glad.

246
00:15:14,903 --> 00:15:16,403
Do you still go to the cinema?

247
00:15:16,653 --> 00:15:19,070
- Please, tell me that you do.
- Of course I do.

248
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:21,986
A lot of people have stopped going.
It's a shame.

249
00:15:22,653 --> 00:15:24,653
You still go...

250
00:15:27,736 --> 00:15:30,070
We could go to the cinema one day.

251
00:15:32,070 --> 00:15:36,736
For me,
going to the cinema with you

252
00:15:36,903 --> 00:15:40,653
was one of the memories,

253
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:44,986
one of the few good memories
I have in my life.

254
00:15:52,570 --> 00:15:54,153
What is it?

255
00:15:54,153 --> 00:15:54,986
Nothing.

256
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:56,570
Something's wrong.

257
00:15:56,736 --> 00:15:58,570
Has something bothered you?

258
00:15:58,736 --> 00:16:01,320
I'm glad
you see it like that, really.

259
00:16:01,736 --> 00:16:03,403
You don't?

260
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:08,320
I guess we have different
memories of that time.

261
00:16:08,570 --> 00:16:10,570
But that's normal, it's fine.

262
00:16:13,570 --> 00:16:15,736
Aren't you going to eat?

263
00:16:15,903 --> 00:16:17,403
I've lost my appetite.

264
00:16:25,986 --> 00:16:28,986
Sorry, but we can't continue
with the conversation

265
00:16:29,153 --> 00:16:31,153
if we don't know
what we're talking about.

266
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:34,653
And I was surprised
by your reaction.

267
00:16:34,903 --> 00:16:36,736
It's silly, really,

268
00:16:36,903 --> 00:16:40,570
you said you had good memories
of us going to the cinema together.

269
00:16:40,736 --> 00:16:43,903
Well, I don't, that's all.

270
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:48,486
You remember, right?

271
00:16:48,653 --> 00:16:51,653
- Remember what?
- When we went to see "Kill Bill 2".

272
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:54,820
- "Kill Bill 2"?
- Maybe you don't remember.

273
00:16:55,070 --> 00:16:56,070
Yes.

274
00:16:56,070 --> 00:16:58,653
When you turned up drunk
and really high.

275
00:16:58,903 --> 00:17:00,653
Excuse me, high?

276
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:03,570
Yes, you ended up fighting
with some guys in front of us.

277
00:17:05,653 --> 00:17:06,653
What?

278
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:09,153
You fought with them
and split one guy's eyebrow.

279
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,570
We got kicked out of the cinema.

280
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:12,570
Do you remember?

281
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:16,653
We came out of the Roxy.
The plan was to have dinner

282
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,986
but you told me you had to go,

283
00:17:18,153 --> 00:17:20,820
You gave me 50 euros
and put me in a taxi.

284
00:17:20,986 --> 00:17:24,486
I walked home on my own
to kill time

285
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:27,736
because I wanted to tell my mother
I'd had dinner with you.

286
00:17:27,903 --> 00:17:29,820
So she wouldn't be angry

287
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:32,403
and say I deserved it
for wanting to see you.

288
00:17:33,070 --> 00:17:35,903
So, I covered up for you.

289
00:17:37,570 --> 00:17:38,320
Have you finished?

290
00:17:41,736 --> 00:17:43,736
What do you want me to say
about all of that?

291
00:17:43,903 --> 00:17:45,320
Nothing.

292
00:17:45,403 --> 00:17:47,153
You come out with all this shit
about me and...

293
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:52,153
I'm not throwing anything at you.
You asked me to tell you.

294
00:17:52,403 --> 00:17:55,403
It's true we went to the cinema,
it's true we saw "Kill Bill 2",

295
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:57,486
it's true a friend of mine
needed my help,

296
00:17:57,653 --> 00:17:59,570
I had to go and see him,

297
00:17:59,736 --> 00:18:00,820
or something serious
could have happened.

298
00:18:00,986 --> 00:18:02,070
I had to see him.

299
00:18:02,403 --> 00:18:04,486
I came back,
you were in the cinema.

300
00:18:04,653 --> 00:18:07,070
I took your hand,
put you in the taxi,

301
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:10,070
I gave the driver the address
and mom collected you.

302
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:13,820
And I wasn't high, or drunk
and I didn't hit anyone.

303
00:18:14,070 --> 00:18:14,986
Ok.

304
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:16,903
And you know what?
It was the Palafox cinema.

305
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:19,070
- No, no, it was the Roxy.
- No.

306
00:18:20,236 --> 00:18:22,320
It was the Roxy, I was
too embarrassed to ever go back.

307
00:18:24,653 --> 00:18:25,820
Fuck.

308
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:29,070
How old were you then?
Thirteen? Twelve?

309
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:31,820
What the hell would you know about
being high at that age?

310
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:34,070
Later on I knew.

311
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,986
Or maybe they put the idea
in your head later on.

312
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:40,320
Don't go there.

313
00:18:40,486 --> 00:18:43,403
Don't go there.
I'm telling you not to go there.

314
00:18:46,153 --> 00:18:46,736
No.

315
00:18:47,403 --> 00:18:48,736
Fuck me, man!

316
00:18:49,736 --> 00:18:53,320
I know someone
who loves telling stories.

317
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,903
I'm telling you not to go there.

318
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:58,403
I just want to know
where that's coming from...

319
00:18:58,653 --> 00:19:00,653
It's coming from reality.

320
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,070
From what I remember
and from what I lived.

321
00:19:03,403 --> 00:19:04,820
You didn't live that.

322
00:19:04,986 --> 00:19:08,070
It's impossible you lived that,
it's something you've been told.

323
00:19:08,986 --> 00:19:10,653
Let's drop it, please.

324
00:19:12,653 --> 00:19:14,653
That never happened.

325
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,653
- They put the idea in your head.
- I'm going to smoke, ok?

326
00:19:40,403 --> 00:19:42,986
Excuse me, sir,
when you've finished

327
00:19:43,153 --> 00:19:45,653
we'd love to take a photo with you.

328
00:19:47,070 --> 00:19:51,070
Of course, but don't call me sir,
just Esteban.

329
00:19:51,403 --> 00:19:52,153
Thank you.

330
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:50,320
I'll keep it on.
I feel a bit cold.

331
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,903
Sorry.

332
00:20:58,070 --> 00:21:00,070
I'm sorry, I didn't want...

333
00:21:03,070 --> 00:21:05,320
- Do you want it heated up?
- No, I don't want any more.

334
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:08,986
I'm sorry, I didn't want to talk
about this, or about anything.

335
00:21:09,153 --> 00:21:11,903
It's all right.
I understand perfectly.

336
00:21:15,653 --> 00:21:18,653
- Are you ok?
- Yes, I'm fine.

337
00:21:35,653 --> 00:21:37,570
I feel bad, I didn't let you eat.

338
00:21:37,736 --> 00:21:40,486
Don't worry,
I'll get something at home.

339
00:21:40,653 --> 00:21:42,736
Will you have time
to eat at the airport?

340
00:21:42,903 --> 00:21:44,236
I'll see.

341
00:21:44,653 --> 00:21:46,653
- Did you get a sandwich?
- I'll see, mom.

342
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:49,070
At least eat something
when you arrive.

343
00:21:49,570 --> 00:21:52,820
Let's see how your hotel is.
Tell me tonight when I call you.

344
00:21:53,403 --> 00:21:56,070
Sorry, I meant,
call me when you can.

345
00:21:56,820 --> 00:21:58,820
- We'll take it as it comes, eh?
- Of course.

346
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:03,320
- Are you sure you're ok with this?
- Yes!

347
00:22:03,570 --> 00:22:05,986
It was just a slip, a silly thing.

348
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:09,570
Apart from you not letting me
read the script or call you.

349
00:22:10,903 --> 00:22:12,320
I knew you'd bring it up!

350
00:22:12,903 --> 00:22:16,320
- I'm becoming predictable.
- Yes, very predictable.

351
00:22:16,486 --> 00:22:18,903
Watch out,
it's that turn-off there.

352
00:22:20,736 --> 00:22:22,570
Yes, it is.
You can't see a thing, mom!

353
00:22:22,736 --> 00:22:23,236
Oh, so it is!

354
00:22:23,820 --> 00:22:25,320
When are you going to get glasses?

355
00:22:25,403 --> 00:22:27,570
When you come back,
I'll have them made.

356
00:22:28,986 --> 00:22:30,653
Ok, it's this one.

357
00:23:02,403 --> 00:23:04,486
Look after yourself, eh?

358
00:23:29,570 --> 00:23:31,070
Water, please!

359
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:41,320
Come on!

360
00:23:42,403 --> 00:23:43,736
Move, move!

361
00:24:13,070 --> 00:24:16,820
Ok, guys. Here they come.
Full concentration.

362
00:24:16,986 --> 00:24:18,236
This is the take.

363
00:24:18,403 --> 00:24:20,320
No extras
looking at camera, please.

364
00:24:20,903 --> 00:24:26,320
10, 9, 8, 7, 6...

365
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:31,486
...5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

366
00:24:45,486 --> 00:24:46,320
Fucking hell.

367
00:24:47,070 --> 00:24:47,986
Captain.

368
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:49,653
- What do you think?
- He's French.

369
00:24:50,903 --> 00:24:52,320
I don't know,
they brought him here.

370
00:24:55,653 --> 00:24:58,153
- They found the plane in Los Lobos.
- Spanish territory.

371
00:24:58,356 --> 00:25:00,320
- It was in Spanish territory.
- I know, you already told me.

372
00:25:00,570 --> 00:25:01,570
How come his throat is cut?

373
00:25:01,736 --> 00:25:02,653
We found him like that.

374
00:25:02,820 --> 00:25:04,070
- We have to...
- What do we do with him?

375
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:05,486
End slate!

376
00:25:05,653 --> 00:25:05,986
End slate!

377
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:07,570
- I'm sorry...
- Don't worry.

378
00:25:07,736 --> 00:25:09,820
Silence, please. We haven't cut.
End slate.

379
00:25:10,486 --> 00:25:10,736
Marking.

380
00:25:11,070 --> 00:25:12,403
11.3. Take one.
End slate.

381
00:25:12,570 --> 00:25:14,403
Now we've cut, thank you.

382
00:25:15,653 --> 00:25:17,403
No, thank you.

383
00:25:18,403 --> 00:25:20,070
Yes, thank you.

384
00:25:20,403 --> 00:25:22,070
Thank you, Miguel.

385
00:25:37,570 --> 00:25:37,820
It's all fine.

386
00:25:39,820 --> 00:25:40,070
It's a technical matter,
very simple.

387
00:25:40,403 --> 00:25:43,070
When Cesar Bernardo turns

388
00:25:43,486 --> 00:25:44,653
first looks at Mercedes.

389
00:25:44,820 --> 00:25:47,570
And two seconds later,
we go to you.

390
00:25:47,736 --> 00:25:50,403
Say the line a little later,
just a second.

391
00:25:50,653 --> 00:25:51,070
I turned too late.

392
00:25:52,070 --> 00:25:52,653
Don't worry. I can adapt.

393
00:25:53,208 --> 00:25:54,736
- I can take a bit longer too.
- No, really, I can adapt.

394
00:25:54,991 --> 00:25:56,986
No, it's a question of focus, ok?

395
00:25:57,820 --> 00:26:01,070
Cesar Bernardo takes us to Salek,
he gets the information, he turns,

396
00:26:01,236 --> 00:26:04,070
we're on Mercedes,
focus on her, two seconds,

397
00:26:04,236 --> 00:26:05,653
then we go to you.

398
00:26:06,986 --> 00:26:10,153
No, say the line when you want.

399
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,403
Malena, just a moment.

400
00:26:13,903 --> 00:26:15,820
She'll say the line
when it's right for her.

401
00:26:15,986 --> 00:26:17,653
We go with her, even though
she's out of focus at first,

402
00:26:17,820 --> 00:26:19,570
and then we keep her in focus.

403
00:26:19,820 --> 00:26:21,403
Don't change anything for me.
I can do it.

404
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:25,070
One thing.

405
00:26:25,320 --> 00:26:27,570
When you arrive,
even if it's out of focus,

406
00:26:27,736 --> 00:26:29,236
look at the Sahrawi women,

407
00:26:29,403 --> 00:26:30,486
their elegance,

408
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,820
their attire,

409
00:26:33,986 --> 00:26:35,653
because for Gabriela
it's extraordinary to see all this.

410
00:26:35,820 --> 00:26:36,820
Even if there's a dead body?

411
00:26:37,070 --> 00:26:39,820
Yes, I think Gabriela is a woman
who observes everything.

412
00:26:40,653 --> 00:26:41,736
A bit like you, I think.

413
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:43,070
- Pablo.
- Yes?

414
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:44,403
No, the other one.

415
00:26:44,570 --> 00:26:45,820
Pablo, how are we doing?

416
00:26:45,986 --> 00:26:49,070
So- so. But Nico is asking
for another hour.

417
00:26:49,236 --> 00:26:50,236
Ok, thanks.

418
00:26:50,403 --> 00:26:52,986
- The camera is good.
- It's very good.

419
00:26:54,903 --> 00:26:56,653
- Emilia?
- What? Yes, I'm coming.

420
00:27:37,236 --> 00:27:39,570
Hello, how are you, love?

421
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:45,653
I'm not calling
so as not to bother you...

422
00:27:45,820 --> 00:27:47,486
But...

423
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:51,820
call me whenever you want.

424
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:54,820
I'd love to have a chat.

425
00:27:55,570 --> 00:27:56,570
Ok, then. Kisses.

426
00:27:56,736 --> 00:28:00,320
And I hope
everything is going well.

427
00:28:00,570 --> 00:28:02,820
I'm sure you're doing great.

428
00:28:09,820 --> 00:28:10,986
Move forward.

429
00:28:11,486 --> 00:28:12,320
I'm going.

430
00:28:12,486 --> 00:28:13,486
Move forward.

431
00:28:15,153 --> 00:28:16,153
Now?

432
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:18,320
Wait, it's very heavy!

433
00:28:21,320 --> 00:28:22,820
Hold on tight.

434
00:28:24,570 --> 00:28:26,736
And pull on the count of three.

435
00:28:27,153 --> 00:28:29,403
- One, two...
- You're not pulling!

436
00:28:30,070 --> 00:28:31,236
Like this?

437
00:28:31,570 --> 00:28:33,236
Am I strong or what?

438
00:28:38,653 --> 00:28:40,236
Ok, cut!

439
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:51,070
...get those boats to port, now!

440
00:29:04,153 --> 00:29:04,736
Pablo!

441
00:29:13,570 --> 00:29:17,070
I need the ropes
to be more tense, please.

442
00:29:47,903 --> 00:29:49,903
Didn't we agree to do it like this?

443
00:29:50,070 --> 00:29:53,403
I can't believe a man in the 1930s
behaves like that.

444
00:29:53,820 --> 00:29:55,236
We already talked about it,
I don't know if you remember.

445
00:29:55,903 --> 00:29:58,486
I remember everything, Cesar,
for better or worse.

446
00:29:58,986 --> 00:30:00,903
Maybe
we didn't talk it over enough.

447
00:30:02,736 --> 00:30:03,903
Miguel, could I have some water?

448
00:30:04,070 --> 00:30:05,486
- Wait, Emilia, I want you here.
- Just a minute.

449
00:30:05,653 --> 00:30:07,320
- It's important for me.
- Ok, I'm listening.

450
00:30:07,486 --> 00:30:08,736
Listen to me.

451
00:30:08,903 --> 00:30:09,903
I'm listening.

452
00:30:10,070 --> 00:30:12,820
- Why don't I say it with signs?
- What do you mean?

453
00:30:12,986 --> 00:30:15,736
With signs, so they're not laughing
all the time.

454
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:19,153
I do believe it.

455
00:30:19,153 --> 00:30:21,820
I don't want it to look corny.

456
00:30:21,986 --> 00:30:24,736
Can we do it as we agreed, please?

457
00:30:24,903 --> 00:30:26,736
I don't think
Bernardo talks that much.

458
00:30:26,903 --> 00:30:31,570
For God's sake, man.
Can't you see everyone is waiting?

459
00:30:34,403 --> 00:30:35,736
- Come on.
- Please.

460
00:30:35,903 --> 00:30:36,736
- All right.
- Thank you.

461
00:30:37,153 --> 00:30:38,320
- Are you ok?
- Everything is clear.

462
00:30:39,320 --> 00:30:41,403
Let's go. We're shooting.

463
00:30:41,986 --> 00:30:42,320
Ok, people.

464
00:30:43,570 --> 00:30:45,736
We're doing another take.
Please, everyone in position.

465
00:30:45,903 --> 00:30:47,320
Can I help you with anything?

466
00:31:01,736 --> 00:31:03,736
Give me two minutes, ok?

467
00:31:04,653 --> 00:31:05,820
Do you want anything?

468
00:31:09,820 --> 00:31:11,820
So, what do you think?

469
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:14,320
I don't see it.

470
00:31:25,570 --> 00:31:26,486
I don't know.

471
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:39,070
Ok, thank you.

472
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:59,403
Let's do a quick sound check.
Can you say something, please?

473
00:32:59,736 --> 00:33:01,070
- Me?
- Yes.

474
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:03,653
Hello, how are you?
One, two, three...

475
00:33:03,820 --> 00:33:05,403
Ok, we've got it. Thanks.

476
00:33:05,570 --> 00:33:06,736
Just a second.

477
00:33:15,986 --> 00:33:18,653
finally in Spain, back home.

478
00:33:18,820 --> 00:33:21,486
I don't know if it was something
you felt you had to do,

479
00:33:21,653 --> 00:33:23,653
or whether you wanted to come back.

480
00:33:24,320 --> 00:33:26,070
It's not something I had to do.

481
00:33:26,403 --> 00:33:29,070
It's just that
the story we're shooting

482
00:33:30,070 --> 00:33:32,070
takes place in a Spanish colony

483
00:33:32,403 --> 00:33:34,070
and the film deals with Spain,

484
00:33:34,403 --> 00:33:37,653
so it was logical to shoot here
and coproduce from here.

485
00:33:37,820 --> 00:33:38,820
I'm very pleased.

486
00:33:38,986 --> 00:33:42,986
But in some way it is different
because you've settled in Madrid,

487
00:33:43,153 --> 00:33:45,736
so I understand
that you're back to stay.

488
00:33:47,653 --> 00:33:50,820
What do you think
the reception will be like?

489
00:33:50,986 --> 00:33:53,653
Your films have always
been well received here,

490
00:33:53,820 --> 00:33:55,820
the critics
have been very positive,

491
00:33:55,986 --> 00:33:57,570
but it's also true
that you were always seen

492
00:33:57,736 --> 00:33:59,153
as the enfant terrible who left.

493
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:01,986
Any film's reception will depend
on what the film is like.

494
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:04,736
And now we have to make the film,
I can't say much more.

495
00:34:04,903 --> 00:34:07,736
But when you left
your profile was...

496
00:34:07,903 --> 00:34:09,736
somewhat controversial.

497
00:34:09,903 --> 00:34:11,903
Do you think
that could influence...

498
00:34:12,903 --> 00:34:14,570
We've answered that one already.

499
00:34:14,903 --> 00:34:16,486
But they asked me to...

500
00:34:17,070 --> 00:34:18,820
Next one, please.

501
00:34:18,986 --> 00:34:21,070
- Let's focus on "Desert".
- Ok then.

502
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:25,070
Emilia Vera, your daughter,
is in the cast.

503
00:34:25,403 --> 00:34:26,903
I didn't know you had a daughter,

504
00:34:27,070 --> 00:34:29,820
I don't think anyone knew,
or that she was an actress.

505
00:34:29,986 --> 00:34:31,736
What is the question?

506
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:35,403
How did Emilia come
to form part of the cast?

507
00:34:35,653 --> 00:34:37,570
Was it your idea?

508
00:34:37,903 --> 00:34:40,320
Was there a casting call?

509
00:34:41,820 --> 00:34:46,570
Emilia joined the production
from her own merits.

510
00:34:46,736 --> 00:34:48,570
But we didn't know
she was your daughter.

511
00:34:48,736 --> 00:34:52,320
That's your business, what you have
to know or not know.

512
00:34:52,486 --> 00:34:54,986
And we don't get to decide
what you write or not.

513
00:34:55,153 --> 00:34:56,570
All right...

514
00:34:57,403 --> 00:34:59,653
Is this where
the interview is heading?

515
00:35:00,653 --> 00:35:02,903
What's it like
working with a daughter?

516
00:35:03,070 --> 00:35:05,903
You're talking to a guy
who has two Oscars.

517
00:35:06,070 --> 00:35:09,736
Are we going to talk about "Desert"
or like this was a gossip magazine?

518
00:35:09,903 --> 00:35:10,986
Thank you.

519
00:35:11,653 --> 00:35:13,236
If it weren't important,
I wouldn't insist.

520
00:35:13,403 --> 00:35:15,986
The distributor keeps calling.
I don't know what to say anymore...

521
00:35:16,153 --> 00:35:18,570
I need you to send me
the audio commentary of "Sirocco".

522
00:36:35,653 --> 00:36:38,320
Hello, I think I can see you.
Is that possible?

523
00:36:39,736 --> 00:36:43,403
Yes, look straight ahead.
Can you see me waving?

524
00:36:45,736 --> 00:36:48,403
Oh, yes, so I can.

525
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:50,070
Hello,

526
00:36:50,403 --> 00:36:53,070
Well, how are you getting on?

527
00:36:53,903 --> 00:36:56,986
Fine, fine.
I'm exhausted, but I'm ok.

528
00:36:57,403 --> 00:37:00,736
That's normal.
It's your first week of shooting.

529
00:37:04,820 --> 00:37:07,736
Tomorrow I'm having dinner
with the actors.

530
00:37:07,903 --> 00:37:10,070
Would you like to come?

531
00:37:11,176 --> 00:37:12,094
Tomorrow?

532
00:37:13,739 --> 00:37:14,212
Yes.

533
00:37:14,236 --> 00:37:15,653
It's a good laugh.

534
00:37:15,820 --> 00:37:20,653
Last week we had a great time
and it helps build team spirit.

535
00:37:23,820 --> 00:37:25,653
What do you think?

536
00:37:25,820 --> 00:37:28,486
I usually end up shattered.

537
00:37:30,736 --> 00:37:35,320
Ok, we'll talk tomorrow,
I'll see you on set.

538
00:37:36,820 --> 00:37:40,653
- Sleep well.
- See you tomorrow.

539
00:37:51,070 --> 00:37:53,820
The U.S. supports you, right?
So that's that.

540
00:37:56,153 --> 00:37:56,653
And France too.

541
00:37:56,820 --> 00:37:58,320
- It's not in anyone's interest.
- Not in anyone's interest?

542
00:37:58,570 --> 00:38:01,320
No, Bilal, otherwise Sahara
would be already independent.

543
00:38:01,403 --> 00:38:04,403
Just think, it has phosphate,
gas, loads of natural resources...

544
00:38:04,570 --> 00:38:07,320
Of course, everyone has an opinion
while you go hungry.

545
00:38:07,403 --> 00:38:09,486
The answer
can't be to occupy my neighbors

546
00:38:09,653 --> 00:38:10,903
who are as hungry as me.

547
00:38:11,070 --> 00:38:12,736
That's a bit of demagoguery

548
00:38:12,903 --> 00:38:14,320
because supposedly
they weren't hungry.

549
00:38:14,486 --> 00:38:15,820
What is it like now, Raul?

550
00:38:19,903 --> 00:38:21,903
- The scale of pity.
- What the hell is that?

551
00:38:22,070 --> 00:38:23,653
You feel sorry for the Moroccans,

552
00:38:23,820 --> 00:38:25,736
but even sorrier
for the poor Sahrawis.

553
00:38:26,486 --> 00:38:27,570
And you shouldn't.

554
00:38:27,736 --> 00:38:29,903
Because they're the ones
who took up arms again.

555
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,820
Because they're desperate.

556
00:38:33,820 --> 00:38:36,820
So half the world
should go to war tomorrow?

557
00:38:37,820 --> 00:38:39,486
Do you think the relationship

558
00:38:39,653 --> 00:38:41,986
between Morocco
and the Sahara is fair?

559
00:38:42,653 --> 00:38:45,736
Do you think the Sahrawis
were better off with the Spaniards?

560
00:38:45,903 --> 00:38:48,820
I don't know, maybe they were
better off on their own.

561
00:38:49,070 --> 00:38:51,153
On their own
and without running water?

562
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:52,820
I don't know, maybe.

563
00:38:52,986 --> 00:38:55,070
Have you asked them?

564
00:38:57,486 --> 00:38:59,903
You should have picked
a Sahrawi actor.

565
00:39:00,070 --> 00:39:03,986
I wanted one, but you came along,
and did a brilliant audition,

566
00:39:04,153 --> 00:39:07,070
you're quite charming
and the wig looks good on you.

567
00:39:07,236 --> 00:39:08,486
It's sex appeal.

568
00:39:10,070 --> 00:39:11,653
Hey, Esteban,

569
00:39:12,070 --> 00:39:13,653
I wanted to ask you a question.

570
00:39:14,403 --> 00:39:16,820
- It's personal.
- Go on.

571
00:39:17,736 --> 00:39:19,403
Why the Sahara?

572
00:39:19,653 --> 00:39:22,570
I mean, whatever a film is about,

573
00:39:22,736 --> 00:39:25,403
there's always a personal theme
for the director.

574
00:39:26,570 --> 00:39:32,236
I don't know, at times you find
the theme after making the film.

575
00:39:32,986 --> 00:39:35,320
But I don't think
four lousy Spaniards

576
00:39:35,570 --> 00:39:38,320
in the back of beyond during
the Republic is very personal.

577
00:39:38,403 --> 00:39:41,320
- And a Sahrawi shepherd.
- And a Sahrawi shepherd too.

578
00:39:42,820 --> 00:39:46,903
If you had to make a film,
what would your theme be?

579
00:39:47,070 --> 00:39:49,070
- I know exactly what.
- What?

580
00:39:49,486 --> 00:39:53,653
My theme would be about
the importance of humility.

581
00:39:54,653 --> 00:39:56,070
Your humility.

582
00:39:56,570 --> 00:39:58,653
- And you?
- Me too.

583
00:39:58,820 --> 00:40:00,653
About humility, of course.

584
00:40:00,820 --> 00:40:01,820
And you?

585
00:40:03,403 --> 00:40:05,820
I'd have to think about it.

586
00:40:06,820 --> 00:40:09,820
About how hard it is...

587
00:40:10,736 --> 00:40:11,903
just to live.

588
00:40:13,736 --> 00:40:14,986
What do you care?

589
00:40:15,236 --> 00:40:16,320
- No.
- Yes.

590
00:40:16,486 --> 00:40:17,403
No, no.

591
00:40:17,653 --> 00:40:19,653
He is his friend,
but he swears he won't tell.

592
00:40:19,820 --> 00:40:23,153
I haven't spoken to him in ages.
You can tell them.

593
00:40:23,403 --> 00:40:25,570
I think it's worse than we imagine.

594
00:40:25,736 --> 00:40:26,820
That's true.

595
00:40:26,986 --> 00:40:29,820
I heard: you grabbed his lapels
and gave him a bleeding nose.

596
00:40:29,986 --> 00:40:31,403
Right, as straightforward as that.

597
00:40:31,570 --> 00:40:32,986
Is that what it was like?

598
00:40:33,153 --> 00:40:35,320
You grabbed him, and bang!

599
00:40:35,403 --> 00:40:36,570
Is that how it was?

600
00:40:36,820 --> 00:40:38,653
That's what I was told.

601
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:41,094
Who told you that?
What are your sources?

602
00:40:41,904 --> 00:40:42,730
Isn't it true?

603
00:40:43,820 --> 00:40:45,486
It isn't true, he grabbed me.

604
00:40:46,486 --> 00:40:48,320
Firstly, he grabbed me.

605
00:40:48,570 --> 00:40:50,736
And then,

606
00:40:50,903 --> 00:40:51,820
what happened, happened.

607
00:40:51,986 --> 00:40:53,986
I already told it, damn!

608
00:40:54,653 --> 00:40:56,820
Did you keep shooting?

609
00:40:56,986 --> 00:41:00,070
Of course,
we still had four weeks left.

610
00:41:00,820 --> 00:41:05,320
His face was all swollen,
he looked like the Elephant Man.

611
00:41:05,486 --> 00:41:08,403
Hours of make- up,
we didn't speak to each other.

612
00:41:08,570 --> 00:41:10,820
Laurette, the assistant director,

613
00:41:10,986 --> 00:41:14,653
she really helped us a lot because
we didn't speak to each other.

614
00:41:14,820 --> 00:41:17,070
She was the go-between,
I'd say to her:

615
00:41:17,236 --> 00:41:20,403
Tell the actor to please
say the line and exit the shot.

616
00:41:20,653 --> 00:41:21,736
And she'd say to me:

617
00:41:21,903 --> 00:41:24,903
No, the actor says he won't say the
line and he won't leave the frame.

618
00:41:25,070 --> 00:41:27,820
That's how it was.
It was a war of egos.

619
00:41:28,403 --> 00:41:30,736
- But the film was finished.
- It certainly was.

620
00:41:30,903 --> 00:41:32,570
The film is fucking awesome.

621
00:41:33,236 --> 00:41:34,486
And the guy is amazing.

622
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:37,903
- Isn't he?
- Yes, yes.

623
00:41:38,070 --> 00:41:40,403
That's thanks to Laurette who...

624
00:41:41,570 --> 00:41:44,736
After that she stopped
talking to me. I don't know why.

625
00:41:46,403 --> 00:41:48,070
For something or other...

626
00:41:54,403 --> 00:41:57,403
I wasn't in a good place
at that time.

627
00:41:58,653 --> 00:42:00,570
But headbutting...

628
00:42:00,736 --> 00:42:03,403
The biggest actor in France.

629
00:42:03,820 --> 00:42:06,403
But we have to understand
that this man

630
00:42:06,570 --> 00:42:09,403
was very rude,

631
00:42:09,736 --> 00:42:13,736
he treated everyone really badly,
especially his assistant,

632
00:42:13,903 --> 00:42:16,653
he turned up late on set,
sometimes drunk,

633
00:42:16,986 --> 00:42:19,986
and one day he grabbed me by
the jacket, started shouting at me,

634
00:42:20,153 --> 00:42:24,320
covered my face with saliva,
and I had to push him off.

635
00:42:26,653 --> 00:42:28,570
You don't believe me?

636
00:42:28,820 --> 00:42:30,820
Yes, of course.

637
00:42:33,403 --> 00:42:38,236
It's a pity Emilia didn't come, and
tell us about a few more stories.

638
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:40,986
What's up with her?

639
00:42:41,153 --> 00:42:45,320
- She's focused on the shoot.
- She's great, eh?

640
00:42:45,570 --> 00:42:47,986
- A hard worker, a good actress.
- Yes, very good.

641
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:54,070
- Vera... is her surname?
- It's her mother's surname.

642
00:42:54,486 --> 00:42:57,070
Do you want coffee?
Excuse me!

643
00:43:12,820 --> 00:43:17,320
Hello, I'm Esteban Martínez,
writer and film director,

644
00:43:17,570 --> 00:43:21,903
and as it will soon be 30 years
since my first film was released,

645
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:26,320
I've been asked
to do the audio commentary

646
00:43:26,653 --> 00:43:28,403
for the BluRay edition.

647
00:43:29,736 --> 00:43:32,320
It's true that the film
wasn't very successful,

648
00:43:32,570 --> 00:43:38,236
so I'm very pleased
it's having a second life.

649
00:43:38,570 --> 00:43:41,070
So here I am, face to face
with these images

650
00:43:41,403 --> 00:43:43,903
and accompanying you
on this journey,

651
00:43:44,320 --> 00:43:46,570
trying to cast my mind back,

652
00:43:46,903 --> 00:43:52,403
while avoiding nostalgia
to the extent possible.

653
00:44:30,903 --> 00:44:34,236
Could I have two bottles
of sparkling water, please?

654
00:44:38,403 --> 00:44:40,653
I'll see if I have any left.

655
00:44:45,320 --> 00:44:48,403
- ...and his name was: Gustavo.
- No!

656
00:44:50,236 --> 00:44:54,320
Gustavo and I
were seeing each other

657
00:44:54,486 --> 00:44:58,153
and after a month I noticed
that money was disappearing.

658
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:02,070
So one day I decided to do a test
and I left 50 euros in the hallway.

659
00:45:02,236 --> 00:45:03,903
We got up the next morning,

660
00:45:04,070 --> 00:45:08,320
the 50 euros weren't there.
I said, it's Gustavo.

661
00:45:08,486 --> 00:45:12,153
My friends said, you have to talk
to him, this is serious.

662
00:45:12,320 --> 00:45:15,236
I was worried about
accusing him of something

663
00:45:15,403 --> 00:45:17,486
that might not be true.
So I said to him,

664
00:45:17,653 --> 00:45:20,070
Gustavo, sorry,
don't take it badly,

665
00:45:20,403 --> 00:45:22,153
but money keeps disappearing.

666
00:45:24,070 --> 00:45:25,320
Oh, I'm really sorry.

667
00:45:25,403 --> 00:45:27,736
This happens to me with
all the girls I've been with.

668
00:45:27,903 --> 00:45:29,153
It's always the same.

669
00:45:29,320 --> 00:45:31,403
I'm a sleepwalker.

670
00:45:32,486 --> 00:45:35,820
I said, a sleepwalker and
a kleptomaniac, motherfucker.

671
00:45:36,903 --> 00:45:39,070
So I decided to put out
Monopoly money for him.

672
00:45:39,236 --> 00:45:42,320
That night I was sleeping,
and I heard...BANG!

673
00:45:42,986 --> 00:45:44,070
I startled you.

674
00:45:46,236 --> 00:45:48,070
I was really worried,

675
00:45:48,236 --> 00:45:49,820
I thought someone
had broken into my house.

676
00:45:49,986 --> 00:45:52,820
I got up, stark naked,
but I didn't care.

677
00:45:53,070 --> 00:45:54,986
I started running
through the house.

678
00:45:55,403 --> 00:46:00,236
And I saw Gustavo,
banging things around.

679
00:46:00,403 --> 00:46:03,070
I said, Gustavo, what's going on?

680
00:46:03,736 --> 00:46:05,070
Did you wake him?

681
00:46:05,236 --> 00:46:09,736
No. And then I said,
Gustavo, Gustavo.

682
00:46:10,986 --> 00:46:12,986
And then the guy....

683
00:46:13,570 --> 00:46:15,570
And I said, Gustavo,
let's go back to bed.

684
00:46:16,320 --> 00:46:19,403
Then I started
leading him back to bed.

685
00:46:19,570 --> 00:46:20,820
And he says, where are we going?

686
00:46:20,986 --> 00:46:22,820
I'm like, out of here,
if you don't calm down.

687
00:46:22,986 --> 00:46:26,070
We went back to bed
and fell asleep.

688
00:46:26,236 --> 00:46:28,236
The next morning I said,
what was all that about?

689
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:30,570
And he said,
when I'm sleep walking

690
00:46:30,903 --> 00:46:31,986
I don't remember anything,

691
00:46:32,153 --> 00:46:34,570
but if you left me Monopoly money,

692
00:46:34,736 --> 00:46:37,403
I must have detected it was fake.

693
00:46:58,570 --> 00:47:00,820
Hi, mom, how are you?

694
00:47:01,570 --> 00:47:03,570
I'm fine.
Forgive me, I'm sorry.

695
00:47:03,903 --> 00:47:06,403
I know it took me
so long to reply.

696
00:47:06,653 --> 00:47:08,820
I've been focused on the shoot

697
00:47:08,986 --> 00:47:11,903
and ignoring my phone.

698
00:47:12,070 --> 00:47:13,653
I'm happy,

699
00:47:14,820 --> 00:47:17,486
I'm happy to be shooting
things I like.

700
00:47:17,903 --> 00:47:19,236
It's really doing me good

701
00:47:19,653 --> 00:47:23,236
to be working
and just being here.

702
00:47:25,903 --> 00:47:27,403
Everything's fine with Esteban.

703
00:47:27,570 --> 00:47:29,736
Don't worry, we're just fine.

704
00:47:30,820 --> 00:47:34,403
It's odd, he seems very different
but we're fine.

705
00:47:35,070 --> 00:47:37,653
He does his thing and I do mine.

706
00:47:37,986 --> 00:47:40,986
But it's interesting
to see him working.

707
00:47:41,403 --> 00:47:45,153
And above all, to see
how he interacts with people.

708
00:47:45,820 --> 00:47:47,653
It's a bit weird,
but I'm doing ok.

709
00:47:48,903 --> 00:47:50,820
Mom says to come for dinner.

710
00:47:51,153 --> 00:47:53,653
Yeah, I'm just coming.

711
00:48:11,820 --> 00:48:13,736
- Ok, cut.
- We've cut.

712
00:48:14,403 --> 00:48:16,986
Malena, the take is a bit soft...

713
00:48:17,903 --> 00:48:19,236
Stand up a little bit sooner.

714
00:48:19,403 --> 00:48:20,903
- Just a little bit, ok?
- Ok.

715
00:48:21,070 --> 00:48:22,070
Let's go.

716
00:48:22,903 --> 00:48:25,236
Raul, can I see you
at the window for a moment?

717
00:48:27,153 --> 00:48:29,570
We're adjusting the focus

718
00:48:29,736 --> 00:48:31,986
and when it's done
we'll be ready to shoot.

719
00:48:32,153 --> 00:48:33,903
- Perfect, thanks.
- Thank you, Malena.

720
00:48:34,070 --> 00:48:35,736
Let's get going...

721
00:48:41,820 --> 00:48:42,903
Hello, can I just stand here?

722
00:48:46,986 --> 00:48:48,320
Silence, please.

723
00:48:48,403 --> 00:48:50,070
We're going to shoot.

724
00:48:52,067 --> 00:48:53,154
- Ey.
- Hi.

725
00:48:53,796 --> 00:48:55,629
Motor.

726
00:48:55,653 --> 00:48:56,903
Sound recording.

727
00:48:57,070 --> 00:48:58,320
Is lunch time staying the same?

728
00:48:58,393 --> 00:48:59,520
71.1.Take three.

729
00:49:00,207 --> 00:49:00,647
Marking.

730
00:49:01,546 --> 00:49:02,462
Frame?

731
00:49:02,486 --> 00:49:03,820
Yes, 2 p.m. or 2.15 p.m.

732
00:49:04,667 --> 00:49:06,667
Action!

733
00:49:12,903 --> 00:49:14,570
Mom says to come for dinner.

734
00:49:14,736 --> 00:49:16,820
Yeah, I'm just coming.

735
00:49:30,261 --> 00:49:30,908
Ok, cut.

736
00:49:31,541 --> 00:49:31,994
Raul...

737
00:49:35,153 --> 00:49:37,820
When you look at your daughter,
I want you to feel

738
00:49:37,986 --> 00:49:40,820
you really need to get out of here,
escape.

739
00:49:41,320 --> 00:49:43,570
Like you can't breathe.

740
00:49:47,153 --> 00:49:48,070
Give me a second.

741
00:49:57,403 --> 00:49:58,820
What is it?

742
00:50:00,653 --> 00:50:01,570
How are you?

743
00:50:02,820 --> 00:50:03,820
Are you eating properly?
Resting well?

744
00:50:04,320 --> 00:50:04,919
We're back!

745
00:50:05,486 --> 00:50:06,009
Yes.

746
00:50:09,736 --> 00:50:11,653
- Do I have something here?
- Nothing.

747
00:50:15,820 --> 00:50:16,736
This weekend,

748
00:50:16,903 --> 00:50:18,403
what are you doing?

749
00:50:18,653 --> 00:50:19,820
I don't know.

750
00:50:20,070 --> 00:50:21,486
Someone from the crew
is doing a lunch

751
00:50:22,070 --> 00:50:23,236
but I don't know what I'll do.

752
00:50:23,986 --> 00:50:25,903
My family is coming.

753
00:50:28,153 --> 00:50:33,986
And I'd love if we could all
get to know each other,

754
00:50:35,570 --> 00:50:37,736
something simple,
meet for a coffee.

755
00:50:38,903 --> 00:50:42,736
Alice would love to meet you.
I'd really like that too.

756
00:50:44,153 --> 00:50:45,320
Can I let you know?

757
00:50:46,070 --> 00:50:47,070
Yes, of course.

758
00:50:47,653 --> 00:50:49,493
What's that you did with,
"Can I let you know?"

759
00:50:50,320 --> 00:50:51,282
- Yes, it's...
- This?

760
