- From the top.

1266
01:30:09,903 --> 01:30:11,236
From the top, of course.

1267
01:30:12,653 --> 01:30:14,236
From the top, without cutting.

1268
01:30:14,403 --> 01:30:15,903
- Let's do some touch- ups.
- No touch- ups!

1269
01:30:16,070 --> 01:30:17,403
She's got shine.

1270
01:30:17,570 --> 01:30:19,820
It doesn't matter,
do like this, Emilia.

1271
01:30:20,236 --> 01:30:20,986
That's it.

1272
01:30:21,320 --> 01:30:22,570
Let's shoot, please,
need to get this shot now.

1273
01:30:23,570 --> 01:30:24,986
Take this.

1274
01:30:25,153 --> 01:30:26,570
We're still shooting.

1275
01:30:27,236 --> 01:30:29,153
That's it, thank you.

1276
01:30:29,570 --> 01:30:30,653
Continue.

1277
01:30:32,070 --> 01:30:34,070
Hold the spoon properly.

1278
01:30:34,403 --> 01:30:37,320
No, not like that.
Hold it like a grown woman.

1279
01:30:37,486 --> 01:30:40,070
Not like a child. Like that.

1280
01:30:42,986 --> 01:30:46,570
She's a young lady from
Madrid high society.

1281
01:30:48,153 --> 01:30:50,570
She's not a working class girl
like you.

1282
01:30:50,736 --> 01:30:52,236
Put down the spoon.

1283
01:30:53,070 --> 01:30:53,820
Ok, again.

1284
01:30:54,153 --> 01:30:55,903
Take the spoon.

1285
01:30:56,820 --> 01:30:58,903
Put it in your mouth. Chew.

1286
01:30:59,070 --> 01:31:00,903
Chew. Swallow.

1287
01:31:01,153 --> 01:31:01,736
Line.

1288
01:31:02,486 --> 01:31:04,153
Keep shooting, please.

1289
01:31:04,903 --> 01:31:06,903
Line, Tim!

1290
01:31:17,403 --> 01:31:19,403
Aren't you going to say something?

1291
01:31:30,653 --> 01:31:32,109
Bernardo, please.

1292
01:31:32,653 --> 01:31:36,070
Not now.

1293
01:34:55,403 --> 01:34:57,070
Is Pepa here?

1294
01:34:57,236 --> 01:34:58,153
The next room.

1295
01:35:00,070 --> 01:35:01,153
Oh, sorry, thanks.

1296
01:35:11,570 --> 01:35:13,903
- Hello.
- Hello.

1297
01:35:13,903 --> 01:35:15,653
Can we talk for a minute, please?

1298
01:35:15,820 --> 01:35:17,736
We're all meeting downstairs
in half an hour.

1299
01:35:17,903 --> 01:35:21,736
I know. I'd like to have
a chat alone before that.

1300
01:35:21,903 --> 01:35:24,653
It will just be a minute,
if that's ok, please.

1301
01:35:26,887 --> 01:35:27,537
Just a minute.

1302
01:35:28,669 --> 01:35:29,141
Alright.

1303
01:35:29,820 --> 01:35:32,070
- Come in.
- Thank you.

1304
01:35:32,986 --> 01:35:35,653
- Shall I close it?
- No, leave it open.

1305
01:35:37,986 --> 01:35:40,653
Can you leave us alone
for a moment?

1306
01:35:41,403 --> 01:35:45,653
Are you sure?

1307
01:35:51,820 --> 01:35:55,653
So, have you decided already
or can I say something?

1308
01:35:58,653 --> 01:36:01,653
But we can talk if you like.
If you don't mind, I'll go first.

1309
01:36:01,820 --> 01:36:04,070
Oh, fine.

1310
01:36:05,986 --> 01:36:09,070
I'm sorry,
I'm really sorry, Esteban.

1311
01:36:09,320 --> 01:36:12,403
You gave me a chance
that not everyone would give me.

1312
01:36:12,820 --> 01:36:14,820
I've learned a lot.

1313
01:36:15,570 --> 01:36:18,153
And I know it sucks.

1314
01:36:18,403 --> 01:36:21,653
But that's why I wanted
to wait and finish the week

1315
01:36:21,820 --> 01:36:24,486
to give you time to find someone.

1316
01:36:26,153 --> 01:36:29,236
We won't find anyone
over the weekend, and you know it.

1317
01:36:29,736 --> 01:36:32,070
You'll find someone very quickly.

1318
01:36:32,236 --> 01:36:35,153
Look, I really appreciate
the apology.

1319
01:36:35,403 --> 01:36:37,320
We're both coming
from the same place.

1320
01:36:37,403 --> 01:36:38,986
The other day wasn't a good day.

1321
01:36:39,153 --> 01:36:41,153
- It was completely fuck- up.
- Yes.

1322
01:36:42,070 --> 01:36:42,903
Completely fucked up...

1323
01:36:43,070 --> 01:36:44,736
Yes, it wasn't my best day.

1324
01:36:44,903 --> 01:36:47,403
I'm anything
but proud of what happened,

1325
01:36:47,570 --> 01:36:51,653
I freely admit it, but
it's no reason for you to leave.

1326
01:36:51,820 --> 01:36:54,403
- Whatever way you look at it.
- I don't know.

1327
01:36:54,570 --> 01:36:56,736
Maybe I'm used to
another kind of shoot.

1328
01:36:56,903 --> 01:36:58,570
What other kind of shoot, Pepa?

1329
01:36:58,736 --> 01:37:01,736
Shoots are like this, everywhere.
Mine and anybody's.

1330
01:37:01,903 --> 01:37:04,653
There are easy days, fun days,
shit days, hard days....

1331
01:37:04,820 --> 01:37:06,570
That wasn't a hard day.

1332
01:37:06,736 --> 01:37:09,986
It was something I never want
to see again, you understand?

1333
01:37:10,320 --> 01:37:13,486
I understand,
and it won't happen again.

1334
01:37:13,653 --> 01:37:16,153
- Well...
- No, it's true, believe me.

1335
01:37:16,653 --> 01:37:19,320
It's down to me, isn't it?
It won't happen again.

1336
01:37:19,570 --> 01:37:21,320
Whatever you say.

1337
01:37:21,570 --> 01:37:22,486
I woke up an hour ago

1338
01:37:23,403 --> 01:37:26,153
to the news that you're leaving
with your camera crew,

1339
01:37:26,403 --> 01:37:28,986
three weeks
before the end of shooting.

1340
01:37:29,153 --> 01:37:32,986
Which also makes me wonder
what the rest of them think.

1341
01:37:33,153 --> 01:37:35,986
Do they agree with walking out on
a shoot like this?

1342
01:37:36,153 --> 01:37:38,903
Yes. If we stay,
we're saying we accept this.

1343
01:37:39,070 --> 01:37:42,570
What is "this"?
What do you mean by "this"?

1344
01:37:42,736 --> 01:37:44,820
All I see here is
a lack of professionalism

1345
01:37:44,986 --> 01:37:45,986
and a lack of respect,

1346
01:37:46,153 --> 01:37:47,903
not for me,
but for the whole crew,

1347
01:37:48,070 --> 01:37:49,486
like I've never seen before.

1348
01:37:49,653 --> 01:37:51,153
Something I can't allow you, Pepa.

1349
01:37:51,403 --> 01:37:53,820
- That you can't allow me?
- No.

1350
01:37:55,820 --> 01:37:57,320
We'll talk about it downstairs, ok?

1351
01:37:57,820 --> 01:37:59,403
Why can't we talk about it
here and now?

1352
01:37:59,570 --> 01:38:01,320
Because you're in my room

1353
01:38:01,570 --> 01:38:03,320
and I'd prefer to discuss it
in front of other people.

1354
01:38:03,570 --> 01:38:05,736
Have you really thought
about this carefully?

1355
01:38:05,903 --> 01:38:07,653
Because I can't get
my head around it.

1356
01:38:07,820 --> 01:38:10,903
You can't understand
someone saying no to you.

1357
01:38:11,070 --> 01:38:12,820
You're leaving me high and dry.

1358
01:38:12,986 --> 01:38:16,320
- I'm telling you I'm sorry.
- Ok, and what else?

1359
01:38:16,486 --> 01:38:18,820
Well, this isn't easy for me.

1360
01:38:18,986 --> 01:38:20,820
It would be really something
if it were easy.

1361
01:38:20,986 --> 01:38:22,986
Well, it's not easy.

1362
01:38:23,153 --> 01:38:25,820
And now, please, leave my room.

1363
01:38:29,153 --> 01:38:31,570
Sure...but you do realize
you're not saying no to me,

1364
01:38:31,736 --> 01:38:34,070
you're walking out on 70 people?

1365
01:38:35,128 --> 01:38:36,620
- I do
- You do

1366
01:38:36,805 --> 01:38:37,546
Ok.

1367
01:38:37,570 --> 01:38:39,653
And I accept the consequences.

1368
01:38:40,653 --> 01:38:43,070
Get out of my room, please.

1369
01:39:03,236 --> 01:39:07,236
Well?

1370
01:39:11,653 --> 01:39:14,653
Nakai, yes.

1371
01:39:17,903 --> 01:39:20,320
Nakai has the same agent
in Europe as Pepa.

1372
01:39:20,653 --> 01:39:22,153
- And?
- He won't come.

1373
01:39:23,153 --> 01:39:24,653
Why the hell not, Nico?

1374
01:39:25,029 --> 01:39:26,629
I doubt he wants to.

1375
01:39:26,653 --> 01:39:28,653
Why's that? Have you called him?

1376
01:39:28,820 --> 01:39:32,070
You're not helping here.
Sorry.

1377
01:39:32,653 --> 01:39:35,986
Let's ask him directly.
Do you have his number?

1378
01:39:36,736 --> 01:39:37,820
- No.
- Ok.

1379
01:39:38,403 --> 01:39:40,320
- How can we get it?
- I've got it.

1380
01:39:40,736 --> 01:39:41,986
Give it to Marina, please.

1381
01:39:42,153 --> 01:39:43,820
Marina, call him, please.

1382
01:39:43,986 --> 01:39:45,653
Tell him to come
as soon as possible.

1383
01:40:59,820 --> 01:41:01,070
Why are you being like this?

1384
01:41:01,236 --> 01:41:03,653
I'm not being any way.
I'm telling you what I think.

1385
01:42:27,070 --> 01:42:29,570
- To the airport?
- Yes.

1386
01:42:29,736 --> 01:42:32,986
- Can I drop you anywhere?
- No, I'm staying.

1387
01:42:36,736 --> 01:42:40,070
Ok, thanks.

1388
01:43:01,736 --> 01:43:04,153
- Hello.
- Good morning.

1389
01:43:09,653 --> 01:43:11,403
- Hi.
- How are you?

1390
01:43:18,820 --> 01:43:20,570
Many people
are still missing, right?

1391
01:43:21,486 --> 01:43:22,070
I don't think so.

1392
01:43:22,820 --> 01:43:24,736
I guess no one else is coming.

1393
01:43:30,486 --> 01:43:32,986
Well, anyway, good morning.

1394
01:43:35,820 --> 01:43:39,153
As you can see, we only had to stop
for two days in the end,

1395
01:43:39,403 --> 01:43:42,570
thanks to this wonderful duo,
Nico and Andrea,

1396
01:43:42,736 --> 01:43:44,903
and to the great Marina Cellier,
who gave their all.

1397
01:43:45,403 --> 01:43:46,903
Thank you.

1398
01:43:48,403 --> 01:43:50,986
So, we're back in action,
we're going to shoot again,

1399
01:43:51,153 --> 01:43:55,153
and we're doing so with a giant,
with James Nakai.

1400
01:43:55,403 --> 01:43:56,820
I imagine you know that already.

1401
01:43:57,070 --> 01:44:00,486
He's an amazing
director of photography,

1402
01:44:01,070 --> 01:44:02,320
a genius.

1403
01:44:02,570 --> 01:44:05,486
And a real professional besides.

1404
01:44:07,653 --> 01:44:11,403
So working with him will be
a pleasure and it will be easy.

1405
01:44:15,653 --> 01:44:15,986
Hello.

1406
01:44:17,570 --> 01:44:19,403
You can sit up here in front.

1407
01:44:21,153 --> 01:44:23,403
I was saying that...
It's ok.

1408
01:44:23,570 --> 01:44:26,070
I was saying that
Nakai is a great guy,

1409
01:44:26,320 --> 01:44:27,736
one hundred percent
behind the film,

1410
01:44:27,903 --> 01:44:31,320
and he's going to bring some
wonderful ideas with him.

1411
01:44:31,986 --> 01:44:36,403
But the important thing for me,
with this meeting

1412
01:44:41,653 --> 01:44:47,070
to thank you
in a more personal way,

1413
01:44:47,236 --> 01:44:50,320
for your efforts

1414
01:44:50,486 --> 01:44:53,403
and above all
for your commitment to the film.

1415
01:44:54,653 --> 01:44:59,320
You've been put to the test,
it hasn't been easy,

1416
01:45:00,403 --> 01:45:03,986
so thank you very much
to all of you.

1417
01:45:08,070 --> 01:45:10,903
And...Anything else?

1418
01:45:11,653 --> 01:45:13,486
The beers at 7 p.m.

1419
01:45:13,653 --> 01:45:15,070
The beers at 7 p.m. That's right.

1420
01:45:15,236 --> 01:45:21,486
We've organized some beers
and snacks for Nakai and his crew.

1421
01:45:21,653 --> 01:45:26,903
I'd ask you
to come by and say hello

1422
01:45:27,070 --> 01:45:29,070
so tomorrow
we can start shooting

1423
01:45:29,653 --> 01:45:32,320
with all
the introductions made, ok?

1424
01:45:39,570 --> 01:45:40,570
Any questions?

1425
01:45:40,736 --> 01:45:43,320
Anything you want to say
or to know?

1426
01:45:47,986 --> 01:45:50,653
Ok, thank you for your time.

1427
01:45:52,736 --> 01:45:55,486
I'll see you later.

1428
01:45:57,903 --> 01:45:59,486
Talk to your captain.

1429
01:45:59,653 --> 01:46:01,070
The French won't have any pity,
like you.

1430
01:46:01,403 --> 01:46:02,653
Talk to your captain.

1431
01:46:03,070 --> 01:46:05,570
The French won't have any pity,
like you.

1432
01:46:06,986 --> 01:46:08,403
Talk to your captain.

1433
01:46:08,570 --> 01:46:10,820
The French won't have any pity,
like you.

1434
01:46:11,320 --> 01:46:12,403
Talk to your captain.

1435
01:46:12,570 --> 01:46:15,653
The French won't have any pity,
like you.

1436
01:46:46,820 --> 01:46:48,486
I like that gesture.

1437
01:46:55,403 --> 01:46:59,070
That gesture
looks natural in films.

1438
01:46:59,236 --> 01:47:00,820
It's an everyday thing,

1439
01:47:01,070 --> 01:47:04,653
it makes the actors
seem less wooden.

1440
01:47:07,903 --> 01:47:09,403
What am I doing?

1441
01:47:10,570 --> 01:47:12,153
I'm ridiculous.

1442
01:47:13,070 --> 01:47:15,653
That's why I direct films.

1443
01:47:22,320 --> 01:47:24,653
That gesture you've just made.

1444
01:47:25,070 --> 01:47:27,070
Do it again.

1445
01:47:30,153 --> 01:47:31,736
Let me see.

1446
01:47:38,570 --> 01:47:40,486
Let me see that gesture.

1447
01:47:41,653 --> 01:47:43,653
I like that gesture.

1448
01:47:45,403 --> 01:47:47,403
Do it again. Do it again.

1449
01:47:48,570 --> 01:47:50,653
I like it because in films

1450
01:47:51,403 --> 01:47:53,986
the actors have to be organic.

1451
01:47:54,486 --> 01:47:56,736
Those little gestures make them
seem less wooden,

1452
01:47:56,903 --> 01:47:58,986
less rigid.

1453
01:48:08,903 --> 01:48:11,736
I'm starting
a new project with him.

1454
01:48:12,486 --> 01:48:15,403
I haven't read it
but it's about a kidnapping.

1455
01:48:15,570 --> 01:48:17,403
Shit, I auditioned
for that series.

1456
01:48:17,570 --> 01:48:18,903
You did? Is it happening?

1457
01:48:19,070 --> 01:48:20,653
I haven't heard yet.

1458
01:48:20,820 --> 01:48:22,903
- Shit, Raul, I hope you get it.
- Me too.

1459
01:48:23,070 --> 01:48:23,986
It would be great.

1460
01:48:24,153 --> 01:48:26,986
- Marta, what about you?
- I'm getting married.

1461
01:48:27,153 --> 01:48:28,153
In May!

1462
01:48:28,403 --> 01:48:31,820
I got married during the pandemic
and I'm celebrating it now.

1463
01:48:31,986 --> 01:48:33,153
A fancy celebration?

1464
01:48:33,403 --> 01:48:36,570
A party in the country,
like a village fiesta.

1465
01:48:36,736 --> 01:48:38,486
I love a brass band.

1466
01:48:38,653 --> 01:48:40,736
- Invite me.
- You want to come, darling?

1467
01:48:44,153 --> 01:48:46,153
Good morning, how are you?

1468
01:48:46,403 --> 01:48:47,736
Good morning.

1469
01:48:47,903 --> 01:48:49,486
Did you sleep well?

1470
01:48:51,820 --> 01:48:55,070
I didn't. There was all this noise,
I don't know what it was.

1471
01:48:55,320 --> 01:49:00,320
Some English guys,
they were fighting by the pool.

1472
01:49:01,070 --> 01:49:03,070
Shit. That explains it.

1473
01:49:03,653 --> 01:49:06,070
How's it all coming along?

1474
01:49:09,820 --> 01:49:14,653
The wind is blowing up
it's going to be cloudy and sunny.

1475
01:49:14,820 --> 01:49:18,403
- So we'll have to wait.
- Exactly, a bit of patience.

1476
01:49:18,570 --> 01:49:20,070
- How are you?
- Fine.

1477
01:49:20,320 --> 01:49:21,903
- Ready for the day?
- All set.

1478
01:49:22,070 --> 01:49:23,653
- It's important.
- Very.

1479
01:49:23,820 --> 01:49:25,736
- Your capitulation?
- The very same.

1480
01:49:25,903 --> 01:49:26,986
How do you see it?

1481
01:49:27,153 --> 01:49:28,903
I love that scene.

1482
01:49:29,070 --> 01:49:31,403
- Any questions?
- No.

1483
01:49:36,070 --> 01:49:39,070
Production is there
for anything you need

1484
01:49:39,236 --> 01:49:40,653
while you're waiting.

1485
01:49:40,820 --> 01:49:42,653
Water, anything. Ok?

1486
01:49:44,820 --> 01:49:47,403
- Yes, thanks.
- No, thank you, always,

1487
01:49:48,653 --> 01:49:50,820
for your patience.

1488
01:49:56,820 --> 01:49:59,653
Well, I'll get going,
just say if you need anything.

1489
01:50:03,986 --> 01:50:05,486
Shall we continue?

1490
01:50:08,736 --> 01:50:09,570
One thing...

1491
01:50:11,736 --> 01:50:15,153
The other day
was tough, I know. But...

1492
01:50:15,486 --> 01:50:17,486
the work you did...

1493
01:50:37,570 --> 01:50:40,570
...but the work you did is amazing.

1494
01:50:44,320 --> 01:50:44,986
Keep it up.

1495
01:50:46,820 --> 01:50:49,486
I'll see you there, so long.

1496
01:51:09,903 --> 01:51:10,986
This scene...

1497
01:51:11,403 --> 01:51:12,570
This scene is probably

1498
01:51:12,736 --> 01:51:15,070
the one people remember most
from the film.

1499
01:51:15,320 --> 01:51:18,236
And the truth is,
it was really tough to shoot.

1500
01:51:18,903 --> 01:51:21,320
It was a very difficult scene.

1501
01:51:25,070 --> 01:51:26,736
The crew had a very tough time.

1502
01:51:28,320 --> 01:51:29,903
The actors, mainly.

1503
01:51:30,070 --> 01:51:32,570
We spent two whole days
in that room

1504
01:51:33,153 --> 01:51:36,570
and we all ended up half- crazy.

1505
01:51:46,736 --> 01:51:48,570
I'm still amazed how these images

1506
01:51:48,736 --> 01:51:50,320
are recorded forever,

1507
01:51:51,153 --> 01:51:54,236
in films, but above all
how the experiences remain...

1508
01:51:54,320 --> 01:51:57,236
the experiences
we lived while shooting.

1509
01:51:58,320 --> 01:52:00,903
How that moment
left its mark on us.

1510
01:52:03,320 --> 01:52:07,236
How that also stays
with people forever.

1511
01:53:58,403 --> 01:53:59,986
What take is this?

1512
01:54:00,411 --> 01:54:02,411
The third.

1513
01:54:08,070 --> 01:54:09,986
May I come in?

1514
01:54:10,010 --> 01:54:11,546
Yes, of course.

1515
01:54:11,570 --> 01:54:13,320
To wait here I mean,
it's impossible out there,

1516
01:54:13,486 --> 01:54:15,070
but I don't want to disturb you.

1517
01:54:15,236 --> 01:54:16,403
- No, no.
- You sure?

1518
01:54:24,570 --> 01:54:26,820
Play the one
at the beginning, please.

1519
01:54:37,242 --> 01:54:39,242
- The third, isn't it?
- Yes.

1520
01:54:41,234 --> 01:54:43,234
Esteban, Execuse me.

1521
01:54:45,820 --> 01:54:51,153
I think this isn't going to change,
and might get even worse.

1522
01:54:56,070 --> 01:55:01,403
We'll wait half an hour
and then we'll shoot.

1523
01:55:02,069 --> 01:55:04,069
With that wind?

1524
01:55:05,295 --> 01:55:07,295
Yes.

1525
01:55:07,611 --> 01:55:10,962
I can remove the dialogue

1526
01:55:13,986 --> 01:55:16,737
and shoot with the wind.

1527
01:55:17,070 --> 01:55:19,403
We'll wait half and hour
but then we'll shoot.

1528
01:55:20,820 --> 01:55:21,986
- I'll get the crew together.
- Thanks.

1529
01:55:28,820 --> 01:55:31,237
Is it okay with you to remove the dialogue?

1530
01:55:33,235 --> 01:55:35,736
Yes, of course. Whatever you think.

1531
01:55:51,301 --> 01:55:53,301
How are you?

1532
01:55:57,035 --> 01:55:59,168
I'm fine.

1533
01:56:07,736 --> 01:56:11,153
I'm pleased
to have sorted everything out

1534
01:56:11,320 --> 01:56:13,320
and to be shooting again.

1535
01:56:15,570 --> 01:56:17,153
What about you?

1536
01:56:19,782 --> 01:56:21,782
I'm fine.

1537
01:56:26,153 --> 01:56:28,320
You've almost finished.

1538
01:56:28,875 --> 01:56:30,875
Two more days.

1539
01:56:31,070 --> 01:56:33,403
You can't wait to leave, huh?

1540
01:56:33,653 --> 01:56:35,070
To be honest, yes.

1541
01:56:35,986 --> 01:56:38,820
I'm looking forward
to going back home and...

1542
01:56:39,820 --> 01:56:41,903
and seeing my mother too.

1543
01:56:45,653 --> 01:56:47,820
Of course.

1544
01:56:53,366 --> 01:56:56,946
- You want a piece of sandwich?
- No, thanks.

1545
01:56:57,142 --> 01:56:58,742
- Esteban, excuse me.
-You want some?

1546
01:56:58,983 --> 01:57:00,983
No, thanks, I'll be right back.

1547
01:57:01,436 --> 01:57:02,662
Ok.

1548
01:57:05,196 --> 01:57:06,423
It's...

1549
01:57:06,663 --> 01:57:08,046
Alright.

1550
01:57:08,070 --> 01:57:11,570
It's very tasty.
Here's a napkin.

1551
01:57:15,143 --> 01:57:16,663
Thanks.

1552
01:57:53,820 --> 01:57:55,736
The other day,
shooting on the beach,

1553
01:57:55,903 --> 01:57:59,153
you said something to Cesar
that stuck in my mind.

1554
01:58:02,153 --> 01:58:03,320
What was it?

1555
01:58:05,070 --> 01:58:07,403
You said you remember everything.

1556
01:58:16,403 --> 01:58:18,320
Unfortunately, I do.

1557
01:58:23,903 --> 01:58:25,070
So...

1558
01:58:27,986 --> 01:58:31,403
are you aware of
what it meant to me,

1559
01:58:35,881 --> 01:58:37,881
all that

1560
01:58:41,320 --> 01:58:43,986
all that pain?

1561
01:58:49,561 --> 01:58:51,561
There are....

1562
01:58:54,320 --> 01:58:56,903
There are lots of things
that you don't know.

1563
01:58:59,653 --> 01:59:02,486
There are things
I don't know about you,

1564
01:59:03,736 --> 01:59:05,986
that we don't know
about each other.

1565
01:59:08,903 --> 01:59:10,153
For example,

1566
01:59:10,403 --> 01:59:13,986
at the time

1567
01:59:13,986 --> 01:59:14,986
when you were a child.

1568
01:59:15,153 --> 01:59:16,820
it was
a very difficult time for me,

1569
01:59:17,070 --> 01:59:19,570
very difficult, really fucked up.

1570
01:59:20,736 --> 01:59:22,736
Very difficult.

1571
01:59:25,570 --> 01:59:29,903
And you've grown up, inevitably,
I get it,

1572
01:59:30,153 --> 01:59:35,153
listening to, and understanding,
just one side.

1573
01:59:35,986 --> 01:59:38,570
No, please, don't do that.

1574
01:59:38,736 --> 01:59:41,653
To be able to answer you
I have to explain it.

1575
01:59:41,820 --> 01:59:43,570
Yes...

1576
01:59:45,486 --> 01:59:48,986
...but you always do the same thing
and I'm not interested anymore.

1577
01:59:50,153 --> 01:59:52,236
You're not interested
in my answer?

1578
01:59:52,403 --> 01:59:53,653
Dad, I am interested.

1579
01:59:55,320 --> 01:59:57,820
Answer me.

1580
01:59:57,820 --> 02:00:00,486
With no narrative
or stories, just...

1581
02:00:01,570 --> 02:00:03,820
...answer me, please.

1582
02:00:06,570 --> 02:00:09,820
Are you aware of what
it has meant for me

1583
02:00:11,653 --> 02:00:13,736
that you aren't in my life?

1584
02:00:28,403 --> 02:00:30,403
Yes, I am aware.

1585
02:00:33,070 --> 02:00:36,403
I am aware of the harm
I've done to you.

1586
02:00:48,070 --> 02:00:50,653
And it weighs heavily on me.

1587
02:03:51,403 --> 02:03:52,653
Shall we watch it?

1588
02:04:01,653 --> 02:04:02,903
This is the best take, isn't it?

1589
02:04:16,570 --> 02:04:18,570
Can you play it from the beginning
with the music?

1590
02:04:18,736 --> 02:04:19,820
- Ok.
- Please.

1591
02:06:53,403 --> 02:06:54,403
Cut!

1592
02:06:56,903 --> 02:06:58,236
Did it go well?

1593
02:07:00,570 --> 02:07:02,653
Take it easy!

1594
02:07:06,153 --> 02:07:07,820
Cut, cut, cut!